  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Service Test Pyramid Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Service Test Pyramid Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Pyramid",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Top to base",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "E2E",
                    "note": "very few, full system",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Component / integration",
                    "note": "fewer, one service",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Unit",
                    "note": "many, fast, isolated",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Going up",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "{red:slower}"
                ],
                [
                  "Determinism",
                  "{red:flakier}"
                ],
                [
                  "Debugging",
                  "{red:costlier}"
                ],
                [
                  "Realism",
                  "{green:closer to production}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Reshaping for Microservices",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Services add a ==contract layer== between them",
                "Little internal logic: the pyramid becomes a ==honeycomb==",
                "A honeycomb is heavy on **integration** tests"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Placement Rule",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Lowest layer wins",
              "items": [
                "Push every check to the ==lowest layer== that can catch the bug",
                "A failing E2E test is a signal to add a lower-level test"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Ice-cream cone==: mostly manual and E2E tests",
                "Few unit tests, so feedback is slow",
                "Suites turn flaky"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Each layer up buys ==realism== and pays in speed and trust. Catch bugs low."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Unit and Component Tests",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Unit and Component Tests",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Unit vs Component",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Unit test==: one class or function",
                "No network or disk",
                "Runs in ==milliseconds==",
                "{blue:Solitary}: collaborators mocked; {green:sociable}: real ones",
                "==Component test==: one whole service through its public API (HTTP or messages)",
                "External dependencies replaced by in-process fakes or stubs"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Test Doubles",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Double",
                "Does",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Stub**",
                  "returns canned answers",
                  "fixed user JSON"
                ],
                [
                  "**Mock**",
                  "verifies interactions",
                  "`verify(client).send()`"
                ],
                [
                  "**Fake**",
                  "working lightweight version",
                  "in-memory repository"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: Order Service",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "App starts in-process: `MockMvc` or FastAPI `TestClient`",
                "`GET /orders/7` calls `/users/1` downstream",
                "WireMock stubs that call; the client base URL points at WireMock",
                "Assert on response body and status code"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "MockMvc",
                    "sub": "GET /orders/7",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "App",
                    "sub": "in-process",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "WireMock",
                    "sub": "/users/1",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@RegisterExtension static WireMockExtension wm =",
                "  WireMockExtension.newInstance().build();",
                "@DynamicPropertySource static void p(DynamicPropertyRegistry r) {",
                "  r.add(\"users.base-url\", wm::baseUrl); }",
                "wm.stubFor(get(\"/users/1\").willReturn(okJson(\"{\\\"id\\\":1}\")));",
                "mockMvc.perform(get(\"/orders/7\")).andExpect(status().isOk())",
                "  .andExpect(jsonPath(\"$.userId\").value(1));"
              ],
              "note": "users.base-url is the downstream client's base URL"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Over-mocking",
              "text": "Tests assert implementation details and break on every refactor. Test ==behaviour and outputs== instead."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Consumer-Driven Contract Tests with Pact",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Consumer-Driven Contract Tests with Pact",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Contract Flow",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Contract test==: consumer expectations and provider behaviour agree, with no joint deploy",
                "{blue:Consumer}: test a Pact mock provider; request and response go to a ==pact JSON==",
                "{purple:Provider}: Pact replays recorded requests on the real service and checks responses"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Consumer test",
                    "sub": "mock provider",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Pact file",
                    "sub": "JSON",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Broker",
                    "sub": "publish",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Provider verify",
                    "sub": "real replay",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Provider States and Broker",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Provider state `given 'user 1 exists'` seeds the data before replay",
                "==Pact Broker== / PactFlow store pacts and verification results",
                "==can-i-deploy== asks: is this version safe against its partners?"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "pact-broker can-i-deploy \\",
                "  --pacticipant web-app \\",
                "  --version 1.4.0 \\",
                "  --to-environment production"
              ],
              "note": "gate a release on verified pacts"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Asserting every field, not just what the consumer uses",
                "Exact values instead of matchers: `like()`, `eachLike()`, regex",
                "Treating Pact as functional testing of the provider"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A pact checks the ==shape== the consumer needs, not the provider's business logic."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Integration Tests with Testcontainers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Integration Tests with Testcontainers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What and Why",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Testcontainers== starts real throwaway Docker containers from test code",
                "Postgres, Kafka, Redis, LocalStack; the {blue:Ryuk} reaper removes them afterwards",
                "Real dependency catches **SQL dialect**, migration, serialization and driver bugs",
                "In-memory fakes like ==H2== miss these"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Java Example",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Start the container, then wire `pg.getJdbcUrl()` into the datasource"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Container static PostgreSQLContainer<?> pg =",
                "    new PostgreSQLContainer<>(\"postgres:16\");",
                "",
                "@DynamicPropertySource",
                "static void props(DynamicPropertyRegistry r) {",
                "  r.add(\"spring.datasource.url\", pg::getJdbcUrl);",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "static = one container for the whole class"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Speed and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Speed tip",
                "How"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Share containers",
                  "==static== or singleton across test classes"
                ],
                [
                  "Local reuse",
                  "reuse mode"
                ],
                [
                  "Stable images",
                  "pin the tag"
                ],
                [
                  "Clean data",
                  "truncate or transaction per test"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`latest` image tag",
                "Hard-coded port instead of `getMappedPort()`",
                "`sleep` instead of a wait strategy"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Pin the tag, use the ==mapped port==, wait on a **wait strategy**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "End-to-End Tests and Testing in Production",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "End-to-End Tests and Testing in Production",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What E2E Tests Are and Cost",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==E2E test== drives the **fully deployed** system via its real entry point (UI or public API)",
                "It crosses {blue:all services} and {blue:all datastores}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Cost",
                "Why"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Slow",
                  "Whole system, real network and data"
                ],
                [
                  "Flaky",
                  "Timing and shared environments"
                ],
                [
                  "Hard to debug",
                  "Which service failed?"
                ],
                [
                  "Bottleneck",
                  "One shared staging environment"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Keep Them Few",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==handful== of critical journeys: **login**, **checkout**",
                "Run them as ==smoke tests== after deploy",
                "Not for every edge case; push those to lower layers"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Testing in Production",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "cards",
              "spec": {
                "cards": [
                  {
                    "title": "Feature flags",
                    "lines": [
                      "Expose to few users"
                    ],
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Canary",
                    "lines": [
                      "Small traffic share first"
                    ],
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Blue-green",
                    "lines": [
                      "Switch between two stacks"
                    ],
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Synthetic probes",
                    "lines": [
                      "Scripted checks, always on"
                    ],
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "title": "Dark launch",
                    "lines": [
                      "Shadow real traffic, hide result"
                    ],
                    "ink": "pink"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "All validate **real behaviour** with ==limited blast radius=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Testing in prod with no ==observability== or fast ==rollback==",
                "Writing test data into real customer records, no isolation or cleanup"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Service Testing Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Service Testing Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Layers",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Unit",
                    "sub": "ms, isolated",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Component",
                    "sub": "stubbed deps",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Contract",
                    "sub": "Pact",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Integration",
                    "sub": "Testcontainers",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "E2E",
                    "sub": "few journeys",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Put each check at the ==lowest layer== that can catch the bug",
                "E2E only for ==critical journeys==, such as login and checkout"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Pact and Testcontainers",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Consumer test",
                    "note": "writes pact",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Broker",
                    "note": "publish pact",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Provider",
                    "note": "verifies",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "can-i-deploy",
                    "note": "gates release",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Real dependency in ==Docker==, started from test code",
                "==Pin tags==, never `latest`",
                "Use the ==mapped port== and a ==wait strategy==, not sleeps",
                "==Share containers== across test classes"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "@Container static PostgreSQLContainer<?> pg =",
                "  new PostgreSQLContainer<>(\"postgres:16\");"
              ],
              "note": "pinned tag"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Production safety net",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Feature flags} and {green:canary} limit blast radius",
                "{purple:Synthetic probes} check live journeys",
                "Metrics and alerts, plus ==fast rollback=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A failing E2E test means: add a lower-level test."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A provider renames the response field `email` to `mail`. The consumer's Pact test only asserts on `name`. Does provider verification fail?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No, it passes.",
                "The pact holds only fields the consumer asserts on, so verification replays those.",
                "A rename of an unread field is not caught."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A Testcontainers test uses port 5432 and `Thread.sleep(5000)`. It fails randomly on CI. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Docker maps a random host port; use `getMappedPort()` or `getJdbcUrl()`.",
                "A sleep is a guess; a slow start fails it. Use a wait strategy."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An E2E checkout test fails because tax rounds wrongly in one service. Where should the fix be tested?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Add a unit test on the tax calculation, the lowest layer that catches it.",
                "Keep the E2E test as the signal."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}